minor type="added" "Data streams: attributes sent with the end of a stream (close(reason:attributes:) on TextStreamWriter and ByteStreamWriter, shown in the reader's info once the stream ends), progress reports for a one-shot sendText, sendBytes or sendFile (onProgress) and for an incoming stream (progress on TextStreamReader and ByteStreamReader, as StreamProgress), and StreamTextOptions.totalSize to declare the size of a text stream opened with streamText"
minor type="changed" "Data streams: cancelling a read closes the stream. The cancelled read throws CancellationError, and later reads throw StreamError.alreadyClosed"
patch type="fixed" "Objective-C data stream progress observations stop when their reader is released and can be cancelled with stopReadingProgress without closing the stream"
patch type="fixed" "Avoid a deadlock when cancelling data stream reads by moving the full native close operation outside the synchronous cancellation handler; cancelled reads still close the stream before returning CancellationError"
